1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:02,600
Every chapter of Nekros
that the crimes were based on…

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:03,970
is from the same user.

3
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:05,170
The name is…

4
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:06,130
Asura.

5
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:08,010
I’m just the messenger.

6
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:09,670
It got me thinking

7
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,650
that the person who doesn’t want
this nonsense to end

8
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:12,800
is you.

9
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,700
You’re not a cop or a reporter.

10
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:18,490
What you are is just a brat!

11
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,360
I’m just a useless thing to you.

12
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,640
You don’t believe in me at all.

13
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,730
(Inspector Yotsaphat Traikanawut.)

14
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,500
(This was also the surname
of Commissioner Praphaphat,)

15
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:29,930
(the Inspector’s very own father.)

16
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:31,410
You knew all this time, didn’t you?

17
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,600
Your father destroyed my family.

18
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:36,900
The reason I chose to be a cop

19
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,400
was because I wanted to remind myself

20
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,300
that I would never make
the same mistake my father did.

21
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,850
(You’re not a cop or a reporter.)

22
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:58,500
What you are is just a brat!

23
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:00,900
Yeah!

24
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,580
I’m just a useless thing to you.

25
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:05,980
You don’t believe in me at all.

26
00:01:47,490 --> 00:01:49,100
(Chapter 20 really is intense.)

27
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:52,500
(But if the next victim
really is in Chapter 20,)

28
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:57,700
(that means there isn’t
just one murderer.)

29
00:02:00,230 --> 00:02:01,690
Who helped you come up with the methods?

30
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,900
I’m just the messenger.

31
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:08,630
I don’t know…

32
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:12,100
But if that’s the case,
it’s interesting, isn’t it?

33
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:26,000
I think…

34
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:30,600
Kim is just a pawn.

35
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:35,980
Someone is working behind the curtain,
pulling the strings and helping him.

36
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:40,400
The number 20 Kim wrote on the glass…

37
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,100
It’s no coincidence.

38
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:48,900
I think it’s the clue to the next victim,

39
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,300
which is in Chapter 20 of Nekros.

40
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:56,680
Right now, Praew is helping me
look for the rest of the manga

41
00:02:56,890 --> 00:02:59,170
from the Nekros fans
in an underground blog.

42
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:02,700
If we get those,

43
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:06,100
we might get some more clues.

44
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:15,470
The police did everything you told us to.

45
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:20,100
But every information we have…

46
00:03:22,230 --> 00:03:23,500
is what you already saw.

47
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:36,210
I don’t think there’s a Nekros fan
who wants to help the police out

48
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:39,700
more than I do.

49
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:56,900
If you don’t believe me, that’s okay.

50
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:02,070
I’ll keep digging either way.

51
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:37,500
Are you here for the interview?

52
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,700
Yes.

53
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:40,250
I’ll fetch the boss.

54
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,300
Wait.

55
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:47,850
The victim in Chapter 20

56
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:51,700
is the mafia who gets away with
murdering an entire family of witnesses.

57
00:05:52,170 --> 00:05:53,440
Since it’s a high-profile case,

58
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,000
I think it won’t be hard to find him.

59
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:57,770
(I got it.)

60
00:05:58,270 --> 00:05:59,100
(This must be him.)

61
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:02,750
(Kamjorn Petchchai,
also known as Big Brother Piaw.)

62
00:06:03,850 --> 00:06:05,000
(I’ll send you the link.)

63
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:10,800
“Prosecutor family murder case concluded:”

64
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:14,500
“Court dismisses contract killing charge.”

65
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,530
Attorney Komkrit was Piaw’s lawyer?

66
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:25,180
(I heard Piaw has a logistic
and recruitment company now.)

67
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,500
If he’s not the victim in Chapter 20,

68
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:30,700
I don’t think anyone is.

69
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:34,480
Oh, you’re on time.

70
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,990
Hello. Hello.

71
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,290
I’m sorry we have to
schedule you at this time.

72
00:06:38,470 --> 00:06:40,360
I’m a busy man. I can hardly find time.

73
00:06:40,780 --> 00:06:41,680
It’s quite alright.

74
00:06:41,710 --> 00:06:43,400
We barely gave you any notice.

75
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,100
Don’t worry about that.

76
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,610
Why don’t we talk in my office?

77
00:06:48,030 --> 00:06:50,100
I had my staff prepare
some drinks and snacks for you.

78
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:51,590
It’s too hot out here.

79
00:06:51,630 --> 00:06:53,210
Let’s talk in my office where it’s cool.

80
00:06:53,250 --> 00:06:54,200
Please come in.

81
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:01,600
(Kaye. I got Chapter 20.)

82
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:03,400
“PLEASE DON’T HURT ME.”
“HEY.”

83
00:07:03,435 --> 00:07:05,170
“HOW COME A PIG LIKE YOU CAN TALK?”

84
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:08,200
(Prim and I are going to his company
to investigate this.)

85
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:11,100
(Once we know anything,
I’ll keep you updated.)

86
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:13,330
PROSECUTOR FAMILY MURDER CASE CONCLUDED:
COURT DISMISSES CONTRACT KILLING CHARGE.

87
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,000
I’ve been through a lot
before I am where I am today,

88
00:07:25,250 --> 00:07:28,120
from bathroom masseur
to valet parking attendant.

89
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:29,990
We didn’t know that.

90
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,700
You need to tell us more about that.

91
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,580
Of course. I will tell you.

92
00:07:33,730 --> 00:07:34,780
-Sir.
-I’ve been through—

93
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:36,330
Thank you, sir.

94
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:39,900
For what?

95
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,600
The pizza.

96
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:44,380
You ordered us some pizza, right?

97
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:46,500
Me?

98
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,200
Yes.

99
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:48,210
I did?

100
00:08:27,050 --> 00:08:28,400
Maybe they got the wrong place.

101
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,290
But go on and enjoy it. My treat.

102
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:31,700
Yes, sir.

103
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:32,950
Let’s go.

104
00:08:40,850 --> 00:08:42,110
My employees are probably
just playing some games.

105
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,100
Don’t worry about it.

106
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:46,100
Tell them to pipe down a little.

107
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:47,490
We have guests today.

108
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:48,400
Yes, sir.

109
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:51,000
Let’s keep going.

110
00:08:51,250 --> 00:08:52,300
Come on.

111
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,200
Hey, man.

112
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:04,570
KAYE

113
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:23,000
Kaye, what’s up?

114
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:26,200
You’re getting good at hiding.

115
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:29,900
But I’m here to collect my interest today!

116
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:32,400
Kaye?

117
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:34,300
Where are you?

118
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,200
Kaye!

119
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:39,500
When I was working as a valet,

120
00:09:39,890 --> 00:09:42,700
all I could do was look at these rich men
leaving their cars with me.

121
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:46,400
I remember thinking
I wanted to be just like them one day.

122
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:49,290
Now that I’m here, in hindsight,

123
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:51,960
I can barely believe
I brought myself here.

124
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:57,100
You’re really amazing, sir.

125
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:58,560
Thank you.

126
00:09:59,550 --> 00:10:00,200
Oh!

127
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:02,800
Oh, you’ve made a mess.

128
00:10:04,450 --> 00:10:07,500
I’m going to the bathroom to clean up.

129
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:08,380
Of course.

130
00:10:08,430 --> 00:10:11,980
Just out the door to the right,
at the end of the hallway.

131
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,700
Don’t wander off.

132
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:17,400
You might get lost.

133
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:19,130
My office is quite big, after all.

134
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:22,000
Your story is very fun.

135
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:23,250
I’ll come back for it.

136
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:24,260
Of course.

137
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,400
Go on.

138
00:10:54,830 --> 00:10:57,670
Guys, let’s get this load over with
before we eat.

139
00:10:57,710 --> 00:10:58,500
Come on.

140
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,900
PHAT

141
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:35,010
I’ll take a little break
to check up on my office.

142
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:37,490
I have to see
if my staff manage the place neatly.

143
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:32,300
Where was I in the story?

144
00:12:37,550 --> 00:12:39,300
Right, right, right…

145
00:12:42,830 --> 00:12:44,570
The world is cruel.

146
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:32,380
(First of all,)

147
00:13:32,850 --> 00:13:34,300
(you need to stop being scared.)

148
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,350
See clearly.

149
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,600
(Don’t look away.)

150
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,700
(If you do,)

151
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:45,100
(you won’t see your enemy.)

152
00:13:45,390 --> 00:13:47,000
(And you won’t see his openings.)

153
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:53,170
(Let your body navigate the flow.)

154
00:13:54,110 --> 00:13:55,900
(Focus on the opponent in front of you.)

155
00:14:03,470 --> 00:14:06,700
(Twist your hips
and swing your leg like a bat.)

156
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:09,200
(Take deep breaths.)

157
00:14:09,930 --> 00:14:13,500
(When they’re not looking,
elbow them really hard.)

158
00:15:09,068 --> 00:15:09,800
Shut up!

159
00:15:12,395 --> 00:15:13,180
Get in there!

160
00:15:17,365 --> 00:15:18,400
You decoys.

161
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:20,330
Who sent you?

162
00:15:22,825 --> 00:15:24,202
We really are journalists.

163
00:15:24,417 --> 00:15:26,896
We’re working on
the Nekros serial murders.

164
00:15:27,029 --> 00:15:28,509
I know you’d be the next victim
so we’re here to warn yo—

165
00:15:28,539 --> 00:15:29,296
Shush!

166
00:15:30,324 --> 00:15:31,300
Nonsense!

167
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:35,201
Nerve…

168
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:37,669
You have some nerve.

169
00:15:37,699 --> 00:15:39,000
Don’t you?

170
00:15:41,512 --> 00:15:45,000
Take these two to a separate room.

171
00:15:47,368 --> 00:15:50,500
Tell our client I have
two extra merchandise for them for free.

172
00:15:51,499 --> 00:15:53,700
It’s freaking exclusive.

173
00:15:54,029 --> 00:15:54,897
Yes, sir.

174
00:15:55,509 --> 00:15:56,700
Go! Get up!

175
00:15:56,819 --> 00:15:57,391
Get up!

176
00:15:58,490 --> 00:15:59,471
Go!

177
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:00,798
Go!

178
00:16:15,582 --> 00:16:16,297
Kaye!

179
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:19,746
What happened?

180
00:16:21,374 --> 00:16:22,896
Hey, stay with me.

181
00:16:23,001 --> 00:16:23,902
Stay with me.

182
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:25,700
I’ll take you to the hospital.

183
00:16:26,949 --> 00:16:27,900
No…

184
00:16:28,798 --> 00:16:29,900
No, Phat.

185
00:16:32,906 --> 00:16:34,402
Look at you, dude!

186
00:16:35,611 --> 00:16:37,900
Phat, listen to me.

187
00:16:38,856 --> 00:16:41,198
Right now, Praew…

188
00:16:43,660 --> 00:16:45,097
She’s in danger.

189
00:17:01,391 --> 00:17:02,197
Thanks.

190
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:07,902
I finally got the information
on the victim Praew sent me.

191
00:17:09,103 --> 00:17:10,099
The victim is…

192
00:17:11,370 --> 00:17:13,297
Kamjorn Petchchai.

193
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:17,899
Oh, that jerk!

194
00:17:18,432 --> 00:17:19,499
I know him.

195
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:22,370
He has endless charges to his name.

196
00:17:24,850 --> 00:17:26,402
I’m an idiot.

197
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:28,801
I know damn well what my sister is like,

198
00:17:29,130 --> 00:17:30,897
and I said that to her.

199
00:17:35,810 --> 00:17:36,845
It was my fault, too.

200
00:17:37,936 --> 00:17:39,097
I didn’t think it through,

201
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,453
and dragged your sister into this.

202
00:17:43,737 --> 00:17:46,696
But Praew also sent me
the location of the victim’s office.

203
00:17:49,410 --> 00:17:51,574
Okay. I bet that’s where she is.

204
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,097
You have some nerve, huh?

205
00:17:54,190 --> 00:17:55,897
Don’t hurt my friend, you asshole!

206
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,000
Prim.

207
00:17:58,510 --> 00:18:00,099
Stay out of the way.

208
00:18:00,630 --> 00:18:03,582
If it’s not your turn yet,
then, it’s not your business!

209
00:18:06,743 --> 00:18:07,900
It’s not your business.

210
00:18:12,891 --> 00:18:14,696
You bitch, you bit me!

211
00:18:16,205 --> 00:18:17,300
How dare you bite me!

212
00:18:18,445 --> 00:18:19,697
You dare bite me?

213
00:18:28,179 --> 00:18:29,499
I said stay out of the way!

214
00:18:33,832 --> 00:18:36,699
This is only for fooling me.

215
00:18:37,463 --> 00:18:38,795
But don’t you worry.

216
00:18:39,407 --> 00:18:41,397
I’ll sell you both eventually.

217
00:18:41,854 --> 00:18:45,299
But right now, I just want to beat you up
until I’m satisfied.

218
00:18:48,109 --> 00:18:49,500
You’re a biter, huh?

219
00:18:53,777 --> 00:18:55,102
You’re a biter, huh!

220
00:19:01,668 --> 00:19:02,598
Your turn now.

221
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,158
Run. Run.

222
00:19:04,408 --> 00:19:05,502
Keep running.

223
00:19:05,712 --> 00:19:06,700
Run. Run.

224
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:11,402
Lay there and stay still,

225
00:19:12,170 --> 00:19:13,997
and I’ll give you a show.

226
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,077
Halt!

227
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,120
Police!

228
00:20:40,308 --> 00:20:41,300
What’s wrong with him?

229
00:21:02,376 --> 00:21:03,099
Nop.

230
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:05,820
Contact local police
and call an ambulance.

231
00:21:05,859 --> 00:21:08,380
Tell them to come to Bangkok Worker
Company as fast as possible.

232
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:11,797
There are multiple deaths,
likely from poisoning.

233
00:21:58,650 --> 00:21:59,400
Praew.

234
00:22:02,382 --> 00:22:03,097
Praew!

235
00:22:04,444 --> 00:22:05,099
Praew.

236
00:22:11,465 --> 00:22:12,602
Praew. Praew.

237
00:22:21,562 --> 00:22:22,776
Praew. Praew.

238
00:22:28,487 --> 00:22:34,290
(Kim’s death in solitary raises questions
regarding police’s security.)

239
00:22:34,607 --> 00:22:36,897
(On a more interesting note,
social media has picked up a connection,)

240
00:22:36,936 --> 00:22:39,870
(pointed out By Mr. Thun of Thun Insight,)

241
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:42,682
(who has dug up the connection
between all all Nekros victims)

242
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:45,402
(to the high-profile
Thai Investment Bank case)

243
00:22:45,537 --> 00:22:47,502
(from 20 years ago.)

244
00:22:47,730 --> 00:22:51,702
(This might be more than
what we thought were murder cases.)

245
00:22:54,527 --> 00:22:56,001
I’ll turn the TV off.

246
00:23:12,622 --> 00:23:16,398
That connection of the victims
to the Thai Investment Bank

247
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:20,601
that the reporter was saying…

248
00:23:22,750 --> 00:23:23,748
That is true.

249
00:23:36,754 --> 00:23:40,697
Before this, I looked through
the information of all four victims.

250
00:23:44,050 --> 00:23:45,297
The businessman,

251
00:23:46,870 --> 00:23:48,197
the Permanent Secretary,

252
00:23:49,510 --> 00:23:50,453
the lawyer,

253
00:23:52,490 --> 00:23:54,100
and MP Jaratphong.

254
00:23:56,110 --> 00:23:59,668
Their names are all
in the Thai Investment Bank case file

255
00:23:59,700 --> 00:24:00,995
from 20 years ago.

256
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,600
Some of them were witnesses,

257
00:24:05,690 --> 00:24:07,100
some enablers,

258
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:11,099
and some got acquitted
because of the loopholes in the laws.

259
00:24:18,110 --> 00:24:18,945
Yeah…

260
00:24:20,743 --> 00:24:25,176
I just realized that all the chapters
the murderers chose to imitate

261
00:24:25,510 --> 00:24:27,395
and all the victims…

262
00:24:28,625 --> 00:24:31,797
are all information
from a user named Asura.

263
00:24:34,623 --> 00:24:36,500
I don’t think it’s a coincidence.

264
00:24:38,270 --> 00:24:40,896
I’ve been trying to contact Asura
for a while now,

265
00:24:42,474 --> 00:24:43,697
but so far there’s no response.

266
00:24:51,630 --> 00:24:52,902
-Hello.
-Hello, Uncle.

267
00:24:53,982 --> 00:24:55,176
I’ll go.

268
00:25:13,940 --> 00:25:16,001
I want you to keep taking your time off.

269
00:25:17,314 --> 00:25:18,402
Take it as a holiday.

270
00:25:19,557 --> 00:25:21,004
You’ve been working hard long enough.

271
00:25:27,310 --> 00:25:28,500
And more importantly…

272
00:25:30,687 --> 00:25:32,404
Praew needs you in a time like this.

273
00:25:40,465 --> 00:25:41,297
Yes, sir.

274
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,900
Don’t worry about the case.

275
00:25:44,874 --> 00:25:47,503
I have men looking for Piaw right now.

276
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:50,903
He will pay for what he did.

277
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:36,250
TITLE: NEKROS CHAPTER 20

278
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:52,450
“BIG BROTHER P. IS THE DEVIL
IN HUMAN DISGUISE.”

279
00:27:58,980 --> 00:27:59,980
How is Praew doing?

280
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:01,552
Is she doing better?

281
00:28:04,573 --> 00:28:05,398
No.

282
00:28:07,576 --> 00:28:09,900
The doctor said her body is okay,

283
00:28:11,162 --> 00:28:13,597
but her mind might not be.

284
00:28:15,668 --> 00:28:17,801
They said she might be
experiencing dissociation.

285
00:28:19,742 --> 00:28:21,402
Dissociation…

286
00:28:22,080 --> 00:28:22,730
What is that?

287
00:28:23,940 --> 00:28:26,383
It’s an automatic mechanism
against stress.

288
00:28:27,514 --> 00:28:29,600
In extremely stressful situations,

289
00:28:30,108 --> 00:28:31,490
the body shuts down.

290
00:28:32,050 --> 00:28:33,597
Even when she wakes up,

291
00:28:34,430 --> 00:28:36,546
she might not remember some moments.

292
00:28:46,031 --> 00:28:47,201
I’m here to visit her.

293
00:28:48,370 --> 00:28:50,097
I’m here to visit Prim as well,

294
00:28:51,619 --> 00:28:53,040
so I thought I’d stop by to see Praew.

295
00:28:54,721 --> 00:28:56,896
I’m sorry for what happened.

296
00:28:58,060 --> 00:28:59,749
Your sister is a promising
young girl, Inspector—

297
00:28:59,770 --> 00:29:01,183
Just shut the fuck up.

298
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:06,496
It’s because of you that she’s like this.

299
00:29:08,875 --> 00:29:11,370
I never asked anyone
to do anything like this.

300
00:29:12,454 --> 00:29:14,804
Prim and Praew did what they did

301
00:29:15,860 --> 00:29:17,400
because they really believe in it.

302
00:29:20,379 --> 00:29:21,100
It’s okay.

303
00:29:21,650 --> 00:29:22,702
It doesn’t matter.

304
00:29:23,804 --> 00:29:27,795
I understand how awful you must be feeling
being unable to protect your sister.

305
00:29:28,567 --> 00:29:30,002
-Phat.
-Listen to him!

306
00:29:31,964 --> 00:29:32,985
What the hell did you say?

307
00:29:33,048 --> 00:29:34,001
Phat, calm down.

308
00:29:36,720 --> 00:29:37,647
Calm down.

309
00:29:41,682 --> 00:29:43,174
I think you should leave.

310
00:29:45,715 --> 00:29:47,001
Excuse me, then.

311
00:30:01,444 --> 00:30:02,610
Tell the team to get ready.

312
00:30:02,986 --> 00:30:04,702
We’re changing our plan.

313
00:30:05,317 --> 00:30:07,185
We’ll focus on Piaw’s case.

314
00:30:09,093 --> 00:30:11,002
Our staff won’t get hurt in vain.

315
00:30:11,317 --> 00:30:14,000
I’ll let everyone judge those scums.

316
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:16,770
We’re burning them to the ground tonight.

317
00:30:24,721 --> 00:30:25,174
Phat.

318
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:26,318
-Fuck!
-Phat, you jerk!

319
00:30:26,346 --> 00:30:27,040
Damn it!

320
00:30:27,071 --> 00:30:28,450
Phat, listen to me!

321
00:30:31,650 --> 00:30:32,700
Take it easy.

322
00:30:33,345 --> 00:30:34,200
Listen to me.

323
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:37,497
Listen.

324
00:30:41,982 --> 00:30:44,902
This won’t help with anything.

325
00:30:46,780 --> 00:30:48,500
You’re only making it worse for yourself.

326
00:31:01,186 --> 00:31:02,002
I…

327
00:31:03,324 --> 00:31:04,360
I…

328
00:31:04,794 --> 00:31:07,182
I’m sorry about your sister.

329
00:31:12,277 --> 00:31:13,697
I just want to tell you that…

330
00:31:16,287 --> 00:31:18,497
you’re already doing a good job
as a brother.

331
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:24,097
As a cop, as well.

332
00:31:48,170 --> 00:31:49,000
Yes, Nop.

333
00:31:49,370 --> 00:31:51,601
(Inspector, we got a lead on Piaw.)

334
00:31:55,050 --> 00:31:56,797
I’m suspended right now.

335
00:31:57,910 --> 00:31:59,051
(You should come anyway, sir.)

336
00:31:59,094 --> 00:32:00,297
(I sent you the coordinate.)

337
00:32:25,537 --> 00:32:28,297
This is the house of the prosecutor
whose whole family was murdered.

338
00:32:28,930 --> 00:32:30,339
Does it look like the one in your manga?

339
00:32:30,912 --> 00:32:31,634
Yes.

340
00:33:20,820 --> 00:33:22,783
Oh, Inspector Phat.

341
00:33:23,979 --> 00:33:25,299
What are you doing here?

342
00:33:26,197 --> 00:33:28,801
I heard you were suspended by your uncle.

343
00:33:36,288 --> 00:33:39,580
I got an order to take over this case.

344
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:42,050
Come on.

345
00:33:43,270 --> 00:33:44,497
No need to look so serious.

346
00:33:44,842 --> 00:33:46,404
Let’s take turns proving ourselves.

347
00:33:47,010 --> 00:33:48,500
I need a big break, too, you know?

348
00:33:52,005 --> 00:33:52,699
Nop.

349
00:33:55,922 --> 00:33:58,198
Escort everyone who’s not involved
out of the area.

350
00:33:58,548 --> 00:34:00,499
Secure the crime scene,

351
00:34:01,831 --> 00:34:03,700
and don’t let anyone touch the evidence.

352
00:34:05,180 --> 00:34:06,097
It’s alright, Nop.

353
00:34:09,390 --> 00:34:11,002
I was already on my way out.

354
00:34:12,082 --> 00:34:14,090
Sorry for intruding.

355
00:34:20,731 --> 00:34:22,200
As the manga creator,

356
00:34:25,189 --> 00:34:27,303
you’re still the prime suspect.

357
00:34:43,814 --> 00:34:44,499
See?

358
00:34:44,746 --> 00:34:47,100
This proves that it’s all Nekros’ doing.

359
00:34:47,635 --> 00:34:49,000
Kim was just a pawn.

360
00:34:49,303 --> 00:34:51,000
The real murderer is still out there.

361
00:34:51,712 --> 00:34:54,096
The prosecutor’s family was murdered here.

362
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:56,601
Everyone in his family was Christian.

363
00:34:56,671 --> 00:34:59,497
It coincides with Piaw’s death
in Chapter 20.

364
00:34:59,945 --> 00:35:03,201
Dying in a bathtub
indicates an unholy baptism.

365
00:35:03,653 --> 00:35:05,440
The baptism of death.

366
00:35:06,060 --> 00:35:09,195
The murderer chose to wash Piaw’s sins
with water and blood.

367
00:35:10,060 --> 00:35:12,401
And the torn out page of the psalms…

368
00:35:12,782 --> 00:35:14,502
That is Psalm 25,

369
00:35:14,634 --> 00:35:17,976
which is the story of David’s plea to God,

370
00:35:18,130 --> 00:35:19,699
asking for forgiveness.

371
00:35:20,792 --> 00:35:25,450
The torn out page is a symbol
that God denies that plea.

372
00:35:26,050 --> 00:35:28,004
And I think Chapter 25—

373
00:35:28,040 --> 00:35:29,200
About that…

374
00:35:31,282 --> 00:35:33,401
Let Kitti and his team deal with it.

375
00:35:38,222 --> 00:35:39,050
What does that mean?

376
00:35:39,980 --> 00:35:42,401
I’m no longer leading this investigation,

377
00:35:43,293 --> 00:35:45,500
and I’m not getting involved again.

378
00:35:47,954 --> 00:35:50,300
And you need to be careful.

379
00:35:51,020 --> 00:35:54,299
Kitti still thinks
you’re the prime suspect.

380
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:58,777
Didn’t I prove myself

381
00:35:59,270 --> 00:36:01,099
that I had nothing to do with Piaw’s case?

382
00:36:01,580 --> 00:36:04,189
I’ve been telling you
there isn’t just one murderer.

383
00:36:04,231 --> 00:36:05,979
That’s exactly why.

384
00:36:08,380 --> 00:36:10,500
It makes you even
more suspicious than before.

385
00:36:13,386 --> 00:36:17,802
Did you know that there’s
a type of murderer called a mastermind?

386
00:36:17,980 --> 00:36:19,250
The one who controls everything.

387
00:36:19,765 --> 00:36:21,699
He wouldn’t get his hands bloodied,

388
00:36:22,451 --> 00:36:25,001
but pull the strings with psychology
from behind the curtain.

389
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:28,090
He borrows someone else’s hands
to do his dirty work.

390
00:36:29,940 --> 00:36:32,299
At least that’s what any police
in this world would think.

391
00:36:33,041 --> 00:36:37,297
Your visiting him that day
wasn’t so you could get some clues,

392
00:36:38,070 --> 00:36:39,700
but it was for you to say your last words

393
00:36:39,841 --> 00:36:41,197
or release him from his duty.

394
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:47,201
Let him die
just to cut his tie to you, his prophet.

395
00:36:59,982 --> 00:37:01,100
What do you think?

396
00:37:04,364 --> 00:37:06,000
Do you think I’m the murderer?

397
00:37:41,983 --> 00:37:43,903
(I’ve got all the chapters of Nekros.)

398
00:37:44,008 --> 00:37:45,577
(I’m sorry I saved them.)

399
00:37:45,939 --> 00:37:47,499
(It’s just… I really loved the manga.)

400
00:37:47,543 --> 00:37:50,499
(Is it possible to meet you just once?)

401
00:37:50,911 --> 00:37:52,780
(I’ll give you all the chapters.)

402
00:37:53,630 --> 00:37:56,998
(I’ll wait for you
at Benice Pub & Bistro until midnight.)

403
00:38:17,397 --> 00:38:18,200
Mr. Kaye.

404
00:38:26,238 --> 00:38:27,802
What a small world.

405
00:38:31,484 --> 00:38:33,100
Mr. Thun.

406
00:38:34,462 --> 00:38:35,099
Yes.

407
00:38:35,808 --> 00:38:36,595
It’s me.

408
00:39:04,674 --> 00:39:05,798
Show me your hand.

409
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:07,410
Just show me.

410
00:39:30,030 --> 00:39:31,903
You didn’t have to do this.

411
00:39:35,364 --> 00:39:36,597
But you’re bleeding.

412
00:39:41,601 --> 00:39:42,299
There.

413
00:39:42,475 --> 00:39:43,179
All done.

414
00:39:50,657 --> 00:39:51,902
Don’t stress about it.

415
00:39:53,670 --> 00:39:55,900
I understand what it feels like…

416
00:39:56,920 --> 00:40:00,600
to be left behind all alone.

417
00:40:04,964 --> 00:40:06,801
I don’t want you to go through that.

418
00:40:16,210 --> 00:40:17,300
Thanks, bud…

419
00:40:20,577 --> 00:40:21,598
For being here.

420
00:40:33,674 --> 00:40:37,380
Maybe Asura is the shadow
trailing behind you all this time…

421
00:40:37,414 --> 00:40:38,530
You just never know it.

422
00:40:38,688 --> 00:40:39,579
You’re me.

423
00:40:40,037 --> 00:40:40,998
I’m you.

424
00:40:41,200 --> 00:40:42,320
No one knows you better than I do.

425
00:40:42,371 --> 00:40:43,176
Shut up!

426
00:40:43,410 --> 00:40:44,300
I’m not you!

427
00:40:45,180 --> 00:40:46,096
Just let me out.

428
00:40:46,411 --> 00:40:48,099
The world needs Nekros.

429
00:40:48,150 --> 00:40:50,499
The world needs someone
to wipe out those assholes…

430
00:40:50,654 --> 00:40:51,699
Those scums.

431
00:40:52,631 --> 00:40:53,400
Kaye, run.

432
00:40:53,665 --> 00:40:54,302
Run!

433
00:40:56,207 --> 00:40:57,697
Did I kill him, Phat?

434
00:40:58,087 --> 00:40:59,401
You’re not a murderer.

435
00:40:59,429 --> 00:41:01,997
I’m going to find out who is behind this.
